_loader.py in adapters/jira/ (directory listing: __init__.py, acli.py, ..., outbound_fields.py — no _loader.py); _loader.py lives at package root src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/_loader.py","The identical bootstrap idiom in the package-root sibling outbound_comments.py:55 uses `Path(__file__).parent / \"_loader.py\"` and is CORRECT there because that file is a sibling of _loader.py — the move down two levels was not compensated","Comment at outbound_fields.py:36 still asserts 'this module is itself exec'd standalone via spec_from_file_location in tests', i.e. the fallback path is intended to run"],"finding":"The relocated adapters/jira/outbound_fields.py keeps a lazy_load bootstrap fallback that points at Path(__file__).parent / '_loader.py', which after the move resolves to the non-existent adapters/jira/_loader.py (the real _loader.py is at the package root, two levels up). The fallback is meant for standalone by-path exec without package context — exactly where it will now fail with an ImportError/spec error instead of loading the loader.","id":"0","impact":0.31,"location":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira/outbound_fields.py:42","norm_id":"nfbbc38ca4117cda1","novelty":1.0,"priority":0.1771,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":["Any exec of adapters/jira/outbound_fields.py via spec_from_file_location in a process where the top-level `rebar_reconciler` package is NOT importable (the exact standalone case the try/except is written for): the except branch runs and fails to find _loader.py."],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Change line 43 to `_loader_key, Path(__file__).parents[2] / \"_loader.py\"` so it resolves to the package-root _loader.py from adapters/jira/.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5714,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows